.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
joe@hal9000:~> \fBkbookmarkmerger \fR\fB/usr/local/extra\-bookmarks\fR
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.PP
Merges all bookmark files stored in
/usr/local/extra\-bookmarks
into joe\*(Aqs list of bookmarks\&.
.SH "استانداردها (STANDARDS)"
.PP
.RS 4
\m[blue]\fBXBEL specification\fR\m[]\&\s-2\u[2]\d\s+2
.RE
.SH "RESTRICTIONS"
.PP
When determining whether a given bookmark file has been merged into the user\*(Aqs bookmarks already or not,
\fBkbookmarkmerger\fR
merely looks at the filename of the bookmark file \- the contents are not checked at all\&. This means that changing a bookmark file which was already merged into a user\*(Aqs bookmarks will not trigger merging it once again\&.
.PP
Also note that in case a user modifies a bookmark which was merged into his setup, the original bookmark file will be left unmodified\&.
